  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nUpper level trough is currently tracking across northern Nevada \nthis afternoon, as a result showers and a few thunderstorms have \nbeen ongoing over the Utah/Nevada border with a cool front over \nWhite Pine County, as well as with the main upper trough over the \nnorthern third of Elko and Humboldt Counties. The 20% to 30% \nchances for storms and showers associated with the cool front will\npush into Utah later this evening, however the 40% to 60% chance \nfor showers and a few isolated storms with the main trough will \npersist through Sunday morning as the trough drifts east. Good \nnews is winds will be much lighter than they have been over the \nlast few days out of the W to NW at 10 to 20 MPH. Sunday and \nMonday look to be quiet days as shortwave ridging transits Nevada.\nTuesday, the next upper level trough will move across the silver \nstate, this time across central Nevada, and this system looks to \nmove faster too, bringing a 20% to 40% chance for isolated to \nscattered showers and thunderstorms for the US 6 corridor Tuesday \nafternoon, departing Wednesday morning. Thursday another shortwave\nridge transits Nevada with quite conditions. Friday and Saturday \nmodels are a bit different with possible solutions, as a trio of \nupper level features have the potential to make sensible impacts \nto NE Nevada, one is a Pacific upper trough, the second is a land \nfalling Pacific tropical system whose remains will lift into the \nsouthwest US. Finally the last is the summertime subtropical ridge\nwhich may want to re-establish over the Great Basin. With all the\npossible interactions between these features shown in the \nensembles forecast confidence is very low so will keep the period \ndry for now. Temperatures will be on a slow warming trend for the \nnext several days, but nothing to drastic a afternoon highs rise \ninto the mid 80s from the mid 70s, and overnight lows range in the\nupper 30s to upper 40s. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in a 20% to 40% chance for isolated \nshowers and storms Friday for eastern Nevada.\n\nThere is high confidence in a 20% to 50% chance for isolated to \nscattered showers and thunderstorms for northern Nevada Friday and\nSaturday.\n\nThere is moderate confidence in a 10% to 30% chance for isolated \nto scattered showers and thunderstorms for NE Nye and southern \nWhite Pine Counties Tuesday afternoon. \n\nThere is low confidence for the long range forecast as model \nsolutions show a high degree of divergence for the upper pattern \nnext Friday.",
